Athena bundles a copy of the engine it runs apps with, and that engine is
someone else's work. This file is the short version; THIRD-PARTY.md is the full
inventory of every package in `engine/node_modules`, read from each package's
own metadata.

pinokiod 8.2.0
  The daemon behind Pinokio (https://pinokio.computer), vendored unmodified under
  `engine/node_modules/pinokiod` and booted as a plain Node process by
  `engine/boot.js`. MIT, per its npm package metadata
  (https://www.npmjs.com/package/pinokiod). The published package ships no licence
  file of its own; this notice is the attribution it asks for. Pinokio and its
  catalogue of apps are not part of this project and are not covered by Athena's
  licence.

Transitive dependencies
  501 packages under `engine/node_modules` — every distinct `name@version` with a
  `package.json` in the tree, nested copies included, counted the way
  `THIRD-PARTY.md` describes — all under permissive licences (MIT, ISC,
  BSD-2/3-Clause, Apache-2.0, BlueOak-1.0.0, Unlicense, WTFPL, and the
  dual-licence combinations of those). No copyleft licence appears anywhere in
  the tree. Exactly one package declares no licence field at all —
  `copy-paste@2.2.0` — and is named here rather than counted as "MIT, probably".
  (An earlier revision of this notice named a second one, `beep-boop@1.2.3`. That
  is not a package: it is the fixture inside `github-from-package/example`, which
  is a file shipped within another package and is left out of the count for the
  reason `THIRD-PARTY.md` gives.)

The apps Athena installs are not distributed with Athena. They are cloned from
their own repositories at the user's request and carry their own licences, which
is what the app's own page in the store is for.
